<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00889</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>96155397-6ece-490b-ba63-9d83f76ef31a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3ff8875e-4e04-408c-9be0-efc5a6eb9089" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c4f6daa0-50bc-428c-8cf5-7a097e999cc1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="\(f(9)=f(16)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(9)=f(4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(9)=f(16)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>1. Function \(f\) gives the temperature, in degrees Celsius, \(t\)<emphasis> </emphasis>hours after midnight. </para>
      <para>Choose which equation or expression represents the statement in function notation.</para>
      <para>The temperature was the same at 9 a.m. and at 4 p.m.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(9)=f(16)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b4bd3db2-dbdc-421d-b42e-bb285b895f47" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="\(f(9)\) &gt; \(f(6)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(9)\\) &gt; \\(f(6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(9)\\)&lt;\\(f(6)\\)&quot; ]">
    <problem>
      <para>It was warmer at 9 a.m. than at 6 a.m.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(9) &gt; f(6)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="98400bad-9f27-4e0d-8430-f67c0ae26c26" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(f(t)=24\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(24)=t\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(0)&lt;24\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(t)=24\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(12)=24\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Some time after midnight, the temperature was 24 degrees Celsius.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(t)=24\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2b429285-9e48-4744-8816-9fc39d073d9a" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;(2, -4)&quot;, &quot;(5, 3.4)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;(-4, 2)&quot;, &quot;(2, -4)&quot;, &quot;(3.4, 5)&quot;, &quot;(5, 3.4)&quot;, &quot;(2, 5)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Select the <emphasis>two</emphasis> points that are on the graph of \(f\) if we know that \(f(2)=-4\) and \(f(5)=3.4\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8a768d37-c781-46a7-b425-c2bc929041e4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="0" data-solution="\(g(-5)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(g(-5)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g(5)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Looking at the graph of the function \(g\), below, which is greater, \(g(-5)\) or \(g(5)\)? </para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A GRAPH OF FUNCTION G. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (−5, 2) AND (5, −3)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5a2c775e319efd946b6bd1f0ba070f76f6ce12ce"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(g(-5)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1237bb5b-2130-4f17-8364-9a5468a6d902" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="There are 82 people living on floor 4." data-solution-options="[&quot;There are 82 people living on floor 4.&quot;, &quot;There are 4 people living on floor 82.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The function \(T\) tells how many people are living on floor \(n\) of an apartment building. What does \(T(4)=82\) mean?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! There are 82 people living on floor 4.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.1-4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2dc2c733-5dfb-4762-81ad-c238a622c7b0" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(T(6)=70\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(T(70)=6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(T(6)=70\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(6(T)=70\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(70(T)=6\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The function, \(T\), gives the temperature of a house, in degrees Fahrenheit, \(h\) hours after midnight. Choose which function notation represents the temperature at 6 a.m. was 70 degrees.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(T(6)=70\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b1d1f02d-f133-416a-a9a6-4be309380f15" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground." data-solution-options="[&quot;The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.&quot;, &quot;The height of the drone after 4 seconds is 2 meters off the ground.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph below represents a function, \(f\), which gives the height of a drone, in meters, \(t\) seconds after it leaves the ground. Which statement describes the point \(f(2)=4\)?</para>
        <figure><media alt="Graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, height, meters. Starting at 0 comma 0, the graph increases linearly. From 2 to 6, it’s horizontal. Then decreases linearly to 7 comma 0."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3192aada43883aac8e77e8ee8af08927d79ed818"/></media></figure></problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
